Explanation:

- In `renderFrame()`, after the WebGL helper has finished drawing (`finalizeDraw`) and just before we return the `<canvas>`, we grab the layer’s `className` (set via the `className` option or defaulting to `"ol-layer"`) and assign it to the canvas.
- This ensures that your customised class (e.g. `"ol-layer-heatMap"`) appears in the DOM and that any CSS targeting it will take effect.
